            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Italian for the rate, then the Italian for the inflation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: i contanti",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "i contanti — \"the cash\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Posso pagare in contanti? Can I pay in cash?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Usually plural: pagare in contanti. The opposite is con la carta."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "contanti is the plural of contante \"counted out\", from contare \"to count\", inherited from Latin computāre \"to reckon\" (Lewis & Short): money you can count in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
